//! The differential harness, shared by `tests/differential_test.rs`.
//!
//! Test-only, and deliberately so: every module here is a *checker* or a
//! *generator*, and none of them is part of the language. Keeping them out of
//! `src/` is what lets `cargo test` own them, and it means `redblue::Value` and
//! `redblue::Error` stay the only public surface a caller has to name.
//!
//! The split is by job:
//!
//! - [`rng`] — the seeded generator's random source, so a counterexample is
//!   reproducible on another machine.
//! - [`generator`] — the corpus families, and the typed random grammar.
//! - [`corpus`] — the corpus on disk: where it is, how an expectation is
//!   written, and how a run is compared against it.
//! - [`vm`] — one program, run on both VMs, compared as one outcome.
//! - [`shrink`] — the reduction from "this fails" to "here is the smallest
//!   program that still fails".

pub mod corpus;
pub mod generator;
pub mod rng;
pub mod shrink;
pub mod vm;
