+/// Almost every seed has to produce a program of its own.
+///
+/// The rule is a ratio, not 320 out of 320, because the grammar is small on
+/// purpose: a statement form, an expression per kind, and six fixed fault tails
+/// is a handful of shapes, so two seeds landing on the same program is a
+/// property of the grammar rather than a defect. Requiring perfection made the
+/// gate a coin toss — a benign collision would fail the run, and the pressure
+/// that creates is to widen the grammar or raise the seed count until the
+/// collision stops happening, neither of which checks anything.
+///
+/// What is *not* benign is the seed being ignored, and 95% of 320 distinct
+/// programs cannot happen by accident: `the_generator_is_reproducible_from_its_seed`
+/// pins the neighbouring property, and a generator that ignored its seed would
+/// collapse to one or two programs here.
 #[test]
